    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 civic is making this really loud, high pitched squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be a belt issue? can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a bad one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a critical component that powers various engine accessories in your vehicle, such as the alternator, water pump, air conditioning, and power steering. A bad serpentine belt can cause a high-pitched squealing noise when accelerating, as it can lose tension or develop cracks, causing vibrations that may be audible to the driver. The noise is typically at its loudest when the belt slips and re-engages with the engine's pulleys, which can be frustrating and potentially damaging if left unchecked.",
