    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so if it's slipping, is that just because it's old or could something else be causing it? like why would it specifically happen when i'm accelerating and not just sitting at an idle?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Slipping can indeed be caused by wear and tear, but other factors can contribute to it as well. Acceleration can cause the belt to slip because the engine's RPMs increase, causing the pulleys to rotate faster and putting additional stress on the belt. This increased stress can cause tension to build up, leading to uneven wear or slippage, especially if the belt is old or damaged.",
